From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:06:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(loader): restore scoped managed model weights on GB10

Upstream base: 0332cc5089137753d3af43d1c643516b4350359f.

Rationale: upstream replaced managed model-weight storage with ordinary CUDA allocations for its TP4 test configuration. Three-rank GB10 loading reaches the 5 GiB startup memory floor after weight preparation. Scope managed allocation to final model weights while retaining the current bounded bounce reader and ordinary runtime buffers.

Quality: checkpoint bytes and tensor dtypes are unchanged. The copy path validates managed CUDA ranges; unsupported devices fail closed.

Tests: Python compilation and diff check passed locally; capped GB10 native copy test and guarded TP3 load remain.

Upstream status: candidate compatibility patch for review after live qualification.
